## Topic ERD / flow diagrams (Mermaid) and `media`

When you create an **ERD**, **flow**, or other **diagram** for a **topic** (PD journal / `00-Topic` work or a top-level `00-*` topic folder under Projects):

1. **Format:** Prefer **Mermaid** (`.mmd` with a `mermaid` fenced block, or a `.md` file whose body is the diagram) so the same source can render in editors and tooling.
2. **Location:** Put files under the topic’s **`media`** folder — **`00-Topic/media`** when using `...\Documents\Projects\PD\00-Topic\`, **or** `...\Documents\Projects\00-<Topic>\media\` when the topic is an `00-*` folder at the Projects root (see `tools/organize-00-topic-folders.ps1`). **If `media` does not exist, create it** (do not scatter diagrams only loose in the topic root unless the user says otherwise).
3. **Single source:** Keep **one canonical diagram definition per variant** under `media/`; link or load from there elsewhere.
4. **HTML / journal:** If the **HTML already has a diagram dropdown** (or similar UI), **render the diagram in that control** by **reading from the `media` file** (e.g. fetch + client render, or server include path) — **do not duplicate** the full Mermaid (or SVG) source again in the HTML body. If no dropdown exists, you may embed or link once as the user asks; still prefer **`media/`** as the source of truth.

Details and path tables: **@.cursor/CURSOR-AI-RULES-CONSOLIDATED.md** (topic diagrams section).
